#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""inkctl: let an agent control a Supernote e-ink tablet over Wi-Fi ADB with direct calls, JSON answers and stable exit codes, without root.

Direct calls come first (intents, content providers, files), then element references from a
snapshot, and coordinates only as the last resort. Every command takes --json.

  status                         connection, firmware, screen size, battery, foreground activity
  firmware [--download]          show the installed and newest official firmware; --download copies it to EXPORT
  routes [PACKAGE]               list, read-only, the device's entry points and which job each one does
  doctor                         check, read-only, that each call this command makes still exists
  note open PATH [--page N]      open a note; N counts from 1, as the device shows it
  note new PATH                  create a blank portrait note at PATH and open it; never replaces
  files ls [PATH]                list a folder of the shared storage
  files pull PATH LOCAL          copy from the shared storage
  files push LOCAL PATH          copy to the shared storage; refuses to replace without --overwrite
  sync tasks                     start a To-do sync and wait until it has run
  sync calendar                  ask the Calendar app to sync
  lasso rows                     open the lasso «⋯» list and read every row, scrolling only inside it
  lasso press ROW                open the list, scroll inside it to the named row and press it
  lasso rect X Y W H             lasso that page rectangle, through Probe's «Run Command» button
  lasso last-insert              lasso the page's last element, such as the last ink write
  ink write TEXT --at X Y        write the text as synthetic strokes on a note under Note/Tests/
  ink strokes FILE --at X Y      insert a saved stroke sample there
  ink save FILE                  save the lassoed strokes as a sample
  ink record start|stop [FILE] --plugin P
                                 record the real pen in a plugin, then save its pen tape (#298)
  ink replay FILE --plugin P     play a pen tape to the plugin, as if the pen wrote it, on the open
                                 test note
  batch FILE                     run a JSON list of ink write, ink strokes, lasso rect and lasso
                                 last-insert steps through Probe in one press; one line per step
  note png PAGE LOCAL            the tablet's own PNG of a page of the open test note, through Probe
  note insert-picture FILE       place a PNG or JPEG on the open test note's page, through Probe
  note insert-text TEXT --at X Y --size W H
                                 add a text box on the open test note's page, through Probe
  note insert-page TEMPLATE --page N
                                 insert page N of the open test note with a system template
  note move-page PATH FROM TO    move page FROM of a closed test note to TO, through Probe's file
                                 API calls, while another note is open
  note digest PATH               whether a plugin can read a saved test note: Probe's MD5 of
                                 the file through the plugin file API beside the tablet's own
  note edit PATH OPS.json        apply the Note Editor's operations to a test note, open or
                                 not, through Device Link's helper, with no screen tap (#312)
  note templates                 the tablet's page templates, through Device Link: system ones by
                                 name, the PNGs in MyStyle by full path; read-only (#451)
  note current                   the note open on the tablet and its page on screen, counted from 1,
                                 through Device Link; read-only (#320)
  lang get|set CODE|cycle        read or switch the handwriting language, everywhere on the device;
                                 cycle goes pt_BR, en_US, es_ES among the installed packs
  screen FILE.png                save what the screen shows
  snapshot                       list the screen's elements with short references, and its pages;
                                 --all reads each list and page to its end, --find X scrolls or
                                 turns pages to an element
  click TARGET                   press an element: @eN from the last snapshot, id:X, desc:X, text:X
  wait activity|file|element X   wait for a condition instead of sleeping (--timeout SECONDS)
  sandbox todoist|google|icloud create|list|clean
                                 the test project in Todoist or test calendar in Google, named
                                 «teste ink-tools»: make it, list what it holds, or delete it;
                                 nothing else in the account is read or changed
  localsend receive|send|stop    a headless LocalSend peer on this Mac (LocalGo): receive
                                 auto-accepts into .scratch/localsend-received over https, or
                                 --http; send FILE...|--text TEXT --to ALIAS|--ip HOST; stop ends it
  wait toast TEXT                catch a short on-screen message that holds TEXT, from the moment
                                 the wait starts: start it, then do what shows the message
  apps                           installed packages
  plugin list                    installed plugins, from PluginHost's provider (plugin ls is the same)
  plugin push FILE.snplg         copy a plugin to MyStyle; the install is then done on the device
  plugin install FILE.snplg      copy, install or update, and prove it: through the Ink Tools Helper
                                 app when it is installed, else through named elements on the screen;
                                 --same-version updates a build of main that keeps its version (#310)
  plugin enable|disable NAME     turn a plugin on or off through the bridge app, and prove it
  plugin action PLUGIN ACTION    run a plugin's own action with no screen and print its result:
                                 account-sync sync [--module calendar|todo], ink-tools-probe run-probe,
                                 device-link edit (through note edit)
  plugin allow NAME [PERM...]    set permissions (default: every one it uses) to Always Allow
                                 through the bridge app, and prove it from the plugin's row
  plugin permissions NAME        read a plugin's permissions in Settings; always sets each to Allow
  plugin uninstall NAME          uninstall through the bridge app, else named elements, and prove it
  font install FILE...           copy .ttf or .otf fonts to MyStyle/fonts, where the Note app's
                                 text-box font menu reads them; refuses to replace without --overwrite
  font list                      the fonts in MyStyle/fonts, by the name the font menu shows
  font remove NAME --yes         remove a font; without --yes, only name its files
  logs [--tag T] [--lines N]     recent device log, with credentials masked; see logs --help for
                                 --level, --package, --pid, --grep, --since, --since-last,
                                 --follow and --plugin
  history                        what this command did: --failures, --command NAME, --since 2h
  tap X Y | swipe X1 Y1 X2 Y2    press by coordinates, the last resort
  wifi on                        over the USB cable, turn Wi-Fi ADB on and connect to it
  wifi off                       turn Wi-Fi ADB off, over the cable; --leave-unreachable with none
  secret set PROVIDER            leave a sign-in secret for Account Sync to take, from standard input, never argv
  secret remove PROVIDER         take back a secret Account Sync has not taken yet
  secret status                  which providers have a secret waiting, with only its last 4 characters
  google login                   sign Account Sync in to Google Calendar in this Mac's browser and
                                 keep the refresh token in the login Keychain; prints only its length
  shell COMMAND...               run a command on the device

click, tap, swipe and note accept --snapshot (add a fresh snapshot to the result) and --screen FILE
(save a fresh capture), so one call shows its effect.

--read-only, or $SUPERNOTE_READ_ONLY, refuses every command that changes the device.
--allow-notes lets files pull and screen read the notes folder or a note on the screen; notes under
Note/Tests/ need no flag.
--trace prints each ADB call to stderr as it runs. --log-paths also keeps full call arguments.
--time prints the run's own time on stderr at its end. $INKCTL_POLL_SECONDS (0.05 to 5, default 0.5)
sets the sleep between the reads of every wait.

The device's address is $SUPERNOTE_ADDRESS, else the first line of
~/.config/inkctl/address (or, from before the rename, ~/.config/snadb/address), as HOST or HOST:PORT. PATH is relative to the shared storage, or absolute.
ADB over Wi-Fi is enabled over USB with `inkctl wifi on` (`adb tcpip 5555`); a restart of the device turns
it off. When the stored port refuses, the port Android's Wireless debugging announces over mDNS
(`adb mdns services`) for exactly the stored address is tried once. When one authorized tablet is attached by USB, every command goes over the cable instead, so
the work goes on with the tablet's Wi-Fi off; `status` names the link.
"""

