each run adds one JSON line to ~/.cache/inkctl/history.jsonl, with the fields:
  time       when the run started, UTC
  command    the command's name, never its arguments
  seconds    how long the run took
  exit       its exit code
  error      the failure's name, or null
  app_before the app in front before the run
  app_after  the app in front after the run
  calls      each ADB call: call, seconds, exit (null when it timed out)
These fields are a public contract, like the exit codes.
The log never holds note content, screen text, file content or credentials.
The address is masked. A call keeps only its verb, unless --log-paths is passed.

